   "evidence": "Tensor.lean:51-56 vs. the definition at Tensor.lean:96-97; `a\u2022S + b\u2022((p\u00b7q)S \u2212 (S\u00b7q)p) \u2208 span q` has the nontrivial solution `b = 1, a = \u2212(p\u00b7q)` exactly when `S\u00b7q = 0`. The author's own witness docstring (Tensor.lean:386) singles out `S\u00b7q = -1 \u2260 0` as needed, and roadmap/SpinStructure/README.md:383-385 shows the same omission upstream.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Scattering/DIS/Polarized/Tensor.lean",
   "fix": "Add `S\u00b7q \u2260 0` to the stated hypotheses and note that at `S\u00b7q = 0` the two structures degenerate (`E\u2082 = (p\u00b7q)E\u2081`); flag it to the humans as a second roadmap erratum alongside the `E\u2082` coefficient, since \u00a70.2 of the SpinStructure README carries the same incomplete hypothesis list.",
   "issue": "The \"Not included\" paragraph asserts that on four-dimensional `V` with `p, q, S` linearly independent and `Q\u00b2 \u2260 0` the conserved, `S`-linear alternating forms are two-dimensional spanned by `E\u2081` and `E\u2082`. Those hypotheses permit `S\u00b7q = 0`, where `spinStructureTwo = \u03b5.bilinMap ![q, (p\u00b7q)\u2022S \u2212 (S\u00b7q)\u2022p]` becomes `(p\u00b7q)\u2022E\u2081` and the span is one-dimensional. Concrete point: Minkowski `\u211d\u2074`, `p = (1,0,0,0)`, `S = (0,0,0,1)`, `q = (1,2,0,0)` \u2014 `S\u00b7p = 0`, `S\u00b7S = -1`, `p\u00b7q = 1`, `Q\u00b2 = 3 \u2260 0`, `p,q,S` independent, `S\u00b7q = 0`.",
   "line": "51"
  }
